  "informal_overview": {
    "1.1": "For 0<epsilon<=sqrt(d)/2: Heun from minimizer tildeO(kappa^(4/3)d^(1/3)epsilon^(-2/3)); ExpMid gamma=2sqrt(beta), minimizer X0, independent Gaussian P0, tildeO(kappa^(5/4)d^(1/4)epsilon^(-1/2)). Both marked INFORMAL; exact3.1/4.1 prevail.",
    "1.2": "For each method, sufficiently small normalized step, EXISTS smooth bounded-condition-number target and benign initial distribution, small epsilon; finite-N accuracy requires table lower rates. Not all targets or all initializations."
  },
  "precise_targets": {
    "3.1": "0<beta*h<=h0; unique invariant; alpha W2^2 stationary<=C kappa d(beta h)^3; arbitrary mu in P2 and every N>=0 transient C exp(-cNbeta h/kappa)alphaW2^2(mu,pi)+bias. General-query C(kappa+kappa^(4/3)d^(1/3)/epsilon^(2/3))log(e+alphaW2^2(mu,pi)/epsilon^2). Minimizer specialization log(d/epsilon^2).",
    "4.1": "gamma=2sqrt(beta), 0<sqrt(beta)h<=c kappa^(-1/4), unique phase invariant P2; stationary position normalized bias<=C sqrt(kappa d)(sqrt(beta)h)^2; finite-time statement uses X0=minimizer, independent Gaussian P0; Csqrt(d)exp(-cn sqrt(beta)h/kappa)+bias.",
    "5.1": "Step-dependent oscillatory target(5.1), d>=2, small h, bounded kappa: Heun stationary and one-step-from-target W2>=c sqrt(d)h^(3/2), KL>=c d h^2.",
    "5.2": "Universal thresholds d0>=4,kappa0>1,epsilon0: EXISTS target/init for given d,kappa,small step; N>=c kappa min(d^(1/3)epsilon^(-2/3),d^(1/2)epsilon^(-1/2))log(1/epsilon). Moderate d^-1<=epsilon simplifies first branch. Does not match upper kappa exponent.",
    "5.3": "Gaussian ExpMid: isotropic stationary bias>=c sqrt(d)h^2; anisotropic exact leading normalized bias (sqrt(beta)h)^2/48*sqrt((d-1)/kappa+1/kappa^2)*(1+O(sqrt(beta)h)); prescribed slow-coordinate init yields N>=c(kappa+kappa^(3/4)d^(1/4)/sqrt(epsilon))log(1/epsilon).",
    "6.1-6.2": "Isotropic Gaussian stationary RLMC/RULMC and PLMC/PULMC k>=2 bias>=c min(d h^3,sqrt(d h^3)); k=1 Euler branch >=c sqrt(d)h. Shared coordinate quadrature essential; uniform k constants.",
    "6.3": "d>=2, small h, EACH method and k>=1 EXISTS benign nu0 (energy and W2 bounded Cd), ALL small epsilon and N accuracy imply Heun d^(1/3)epsilon^-2/3; ExpMid d^(1/4)epsilon^-1/2; randomized and k>=2 Poisson d^(1/3)epsilon^-1/3; k1Euler d^(1/2)epsilon^-1. Under gamma2/Gaussian P0 independent; initial law does not depend epsilon/N. kappa bounded examples."
